\@writefile{lof}{\defcounter {refsection}{0}\relax }\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.12}{\ignorespaces A comparison of two CMS software package releases, showing the ROC for the BvAll discriminator of the \textsf  {DeepJet} algorithm (here referred to as \textsf  {DeepFlavour}, an earlier iteration of the name). Seperate curves are shown for c jets and light (DUSG) jets since the respective misidentification rates are significantly different. In the central panel, the filled markers represent the CMS software release that is being validated, while the unfilled markers represent the reference release. The additional panels below and on the right show the ratio between the two.\relax }}{37}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ValidationBvAll}{{3.12}{37}{A comparison of two CMS software package releases, showing the ROC for the BvAll discriminator of the \textsf {DeepJet} algorithm (here referred to as \textsf {DeepFlavour}, an earlier iteration of the name). Seperate curves are shown for \cjet s and light (DUSG) jets since the respective misidentification rates are significantly different. In the central panel, the filled markers represent the CMS software release that is being validated, while the unfilled markers represent the reference release. The additional panels below and on the right show the ratio between the two.\relax }{figure.caption.28}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\defcounter {refsection}{0}\relax }\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.13}{\ignorespaces A comparison of two CMS software package releases, showing the ROC for the CvsB and CvsL discriminator of the \textsf  {DeepJet} algorithm (here referred to as \textsf  {DeepFlavour}, an earlier iteration of the name). In the central panel, the filled markers represent the CMS software release that is being validated, while the unfilled markers represent the reference release. The additional panels below and on the right show the ratio between the two.\relax }}{37}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ValidationCvX}{{3.13}{37}{A comparison of two CMS software package releases, showing the ROC for the CvsB and CvsL discriminator of the \textsf {DeepJet} algorithm (here referred to as \textsf {DeepFlavour}, an earlier iteration of the name). In the central panel, the filled markers represent the CMS software release that is being validated, while the unfilled markers represent the reference release. The additional panels below and on the right show the ratio between the two.\relax }{figure.caption.29}{}}
