\@writefile{lof}{\defcounter {refsection}{0}\relax }\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.13}{\ignorespaces The unrolled discriminator distributions for the jet-driven approach. These represent the CvsB discriminator, in three bins of the CvsL discriminator, for the selected jet of the reconstructed cH(ZZ$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rightarrow 4\mu $)\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}candidates. It is shown once inclusively in the Higgs boson candidate mass spectrum and once with Higgs boson candidate mass criteria applied. As seen in the lower panel of both figures, the relative contribution of a cH(ZZ$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rightarrow 4\mu $)\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}signal with respect to the background estimation generally increases with increasing bin number in both distributions. The region most enriched with signal are the right-most bins of both distributions. This is as expected, since these bins correspond to selected jets with both a high CvsL and CvsB value. Here, the cH(ZZ$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rightarrow 4\mu $)\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}signal contribution is scaled by a factor of $10^{2}$ to improve its visibility.\relax }}{68}{figure.caption.58}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:UnrolledDiscs}{{4.13}{68}{The unrolled discriminator distributions for the jet-driven approach. These represent the CvsB discriminator, in three bins of the CvsL discriminator, for the selected jet of the reconstructed \cHZZ candidates. It is shown once inclusively in the Higgs boson candidate mass spectrum and once with Higgs boson candidate mass criteria applied. As seen in the lower panel of both figures, the relative contribution of a \cHZZ signal with respect to the background estimation generally increases with increasing bin number in both distributions. The region most enriched with signal are the right-most bins of both distributions. This is as expected, since these bins correspond to selected jets with both a high CvsL and CvsB value. Here, the \cHZZ signal contribution is scaled by a factor of $10^{2}$ to improve its visibility.\relax }{figure.caption.58}{}}
